; `light_color` with out-of-gamut components (negative + >1) — the format
; validator (v.color) only checks the Color(r,g,b,a) 4-number shape, not the
; component range, so this lints completely clean. Renders without crashing:
; THREE.Color.setRGB accepts any float, clamping happens only at the final
; framebuffer, matching Godot's own HDR-ish light color handling.

